Description: Hardware control for Acer Predator systems
 Fan control, keyboard lighting, guarded performance controls and telemetry on Acer gaming
 laptops, with no vendor software and no Windows.
 .
 An independent, from-scratch interoperability implementation of the gaming WMI
 protocol, verified against real firmware. Where a control is accepted by the
 firmware but has no observable effect on a given model, this software says so
 rather than implying it works.
 .
 Ships a CLI (alien), a terminal UI (alien-tui), a desktop app (alien-gui) and
 the privileged helper (alien-daemon) that owns the firmware interface so the
 frontends can stay unprivileged.
